WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:05.292
How do you find an inverse using only row
operations? You can perform elementary row

00:05.292 --> 00:10.583
operations. In this lesson we find an
inverse by row reducing an augmented

00:10.583 --> 00:15.875
matrix. By the end, Find an inverse with
the extended Gauss algorithm.

00:15.875 --> 00:20.559
Form the augmented matrix A next to the
identity, then row reduce until the left

00:20.559 --> 00:25.243
block becomes the identity. The right
block is the inverse.

00:25.243 --> 00:30.195
For the matrix two one five three, write
it beside the two by two identity.

00:30.195 --> 00:33.076
After row reduction, the right block is
three minus one minus five two, the

00:33.076 --> 00:35.957
inverse.

00:35.957 --> 00:40.716
A common mistake is to stop before the
left block is the identity. Pause and

00:40.716 --> 00:45.475
decide whether that is right. Reduce fully
to the identity on the left.

00:45.475 --> 00:49.412
Your turn. Find the inverse of one two
zero one. Pause the video. Hint: Clear the

00:49.412 --> 00:53.349
entry below the leading one.

00:53.349 --> 00:58.599
The inverse is one minus two zero one. In
a new context, A zero row on the left

00:58.599 --> 01:03.848
means the matrix is singular. Rate your
confidence from one to five.

01:03.848 --> 01:07.209
Augment with the identity, row reduce, and
read the inverse from the right block.

01:07.209 --> 01:10.571
That completes the course.
